@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g5-inspectors`
IMPORT `g5-senior-inspector`
IMPORT `g5-testing-bodies`
IMPORT `g5-test-conduct`
IMPORT `g5-withdrawal`

-- ind-b-tests-g5.l4: INDEPENDENT tests (author ind-b) of ss.30 to 40 (inspection).
-- Every expected value comes from work/ind-b/expectations.md, written from the sources BEFORE the encoding
-- was opened; the scenario id is given beside each assertion.  Inputs the encoding needs that a scenario does
-- not state are supplied as stated assumptions in the fixtures (the Law has commenced for the work supervised;
-- the authorisation is in force).  Nothing here was edited to match the code; failing assertions live in
-- ind-b-tests-disagree.l4 and ind-b-tests-ambiguous.l4.

§ `ind-b: independent tests of sections 30 to 40`

§§ `Fixtures`

GIVEN c IS A BOOLEAN, p IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Record of offences`
`ind-b record: convicted of a criminal offence` c `, charged and no final judgment` p MEANS
    `Record of offences` WITH
        `convicted of a criminal offence` IS c
        `convicted of a disciplinary offence` IS FALSE
        `charged with a criminal offence and no final judgment yet` IS p
        `a disciplinary complaint is pending with no final judgment` IS FALSE

GIVEN e IS A BOOLEAN, c IS A BOOLEAN, p IS A BOOLEAN, u IS A BOOLEAN, t IS A BOOLEAN, f IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Candidate for authorisation as an inspector`
`ind-b inspector candidate: Ministry employee` e `, convicted` c `, charged` p `, unfit in the Minister's opinion` u `, trained` t `, further conditions` f MEANS
    `Candidate for authorisation as an inspector` WITH
        `an employee of the Ministry` IS e
        `record of offences` IS `ind-b record: convicted of a criminal offence` c `, charged and no final judgment` p
        `in the Minister's opinion an offence of which the candidate was convicted makes him unfit to serve as an inspector` IS u
        `received the training the Minister directed in the field of the powers he will hold` IS t
        `meets the further conditions of eligibility, if the Minister directed any` IS f

GIVEN ps IS A LIST OF `Power of supervision under section 31`
      od IS A BOOLEAN
      bv IS A BOOLEAN
      cs IS A BOOLEAN
      dm IS A BOOLEAN
      sh IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `An inspector at work`
`ind-b inspector with powers` ps `, on duty` od `, badge visible` bv `, certificate signed by the Minister` cs `, certificate demanded` dm `, shown` sh MEANS
    `An inspector at work` WITH
        `authorised by the Minister as an inspector under section 30(a)` IS TRUE
        `powers conferred by the authorisation` IS ps
        `acting to supervise the implementation of the Law` IS TRUE
        `performing his function` IS od
        `visibly wearing a badge` IS bv
        `the badge identifies him and his function` IS TRUE
        `holding a certificate signed by the Minister` IS cs
        `the certificate states his function and his powers as an inspector` IS TRUE
        `the certificate was demanded` IS dm
        `the certificate was shown on demand` IS sh
        `the Law has commenced for the work on the system being supervised` IS TRUE

GIVETH A LIST OF `Power of supervision under section 31`
`ind-b all powers` MEANS
    LIST `require name, address and identification`, `require information or a document`, `enter a place to supervise`, `make measurements and tests`, `order measurements and tests kept`, `deal with measurements and tests otherwise`

GIVETH AN `An inspector at work`
`ind-b a fully equipped inspector` MEANS
    `ind-b inspector with powers` `ind-b all powers` `, on duty` TRUE `, badge visible` TRUE `, certificate signed by the Minister` TRUE `, certificate demanded` FALSE `, shown` FALSE

GIVEN g1 IS A BOOLEAN, g2 IS A BOOLEAN, dw IS A BOOLEAN, co IS A BOOLEAN, cn IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Place an inspector means to enter`
`ind-b place: grounds of unlicensed work` g1 `, grounds of engaging the unlicensed` g2 `, a dwelling` dw `, court order` co `, occupier consents` cn MEANS
    `Place an inspector means to enter` WITH
        `reason to suppose that a person operating there does work on a cooling system without a licence or not in accordance with the conditions of his licence` IS g1
        `reason to suppose that a person operating there engages another in such work without a licence or not in accordance with the conditions of the licence` IS g2
        `used as a dwelling` IS dw
        `a court order permits the entry` IS co
        `the holder consented to the entry` IS cn

GIVEN conc IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Demand under section 31(2)`
`ind-b a demand for a document, the person concerned` conc MEANS
    `Demand under section 31(2)` WITH
        `the inspector demanded it` IS TRUE
        `the thing demanded` IS `a document that is not computer output`
        `the person from whom it was demanded is concerned in the matter` IS conc
        `it secures or eases the implementation of the provisions of the Law` IS TRUE

GIVEN emp IS A BOOLEAN, eng IS A BOOLEAN, at IS A BOOLEAN, ao IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Person who may be a tester or an expert`
`ind-b person: employee of a testing body` emp `, engaged under 34(b)` eng `, authorised to test` at `, authorised to give opinions` ao MEANS
    `Person who may be a tester or an expert` WITH
        `an employee of a testing body` IS emp
        `engaged to be relied on under section 34(b)` IS eng
        `authorised by the Minister under section 36 to carry out auxiliary tests` IS at
        `authorised by the Minister under section 36 to give expert opinions` IS ao

GIVEN who IS A `Person who may be a tester or an expert`
GIVETH A `Test under section 33`
`ind-b an auxiliary test by` who MEANS
    `Test under section 33` WITH
        `performed by` IS who
        `performed at the requirement of the senior inspector` IS TRUE
        `performed on the basis of a list` IS TRUE
        `the list` IS `List used in a test under section 33` WITH `set by the senior inspector` IS TRUE, `set for the carrying out of an auxiliary test` IS TRUE

GIVEN c IS A BOOLEAN, cu IS A BOOLEAN, ch IS A BOOLEAN, su IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Standing as to offences (ss 35 and 36)`
`ind-b standing: convicted` c `, the conviction unfitting` cu `, charged` ch `, the charge unfitting` su MEANS
    `Standing as to offences (ss 35 and 36)` WITH
        `record of offences` IS `ind-b record: convicted of a criminal offence` c `, charged and no final judgment` ch
        `a conviction is for an offence that makes the person unfit` IS cu
        `the offence suspected in a pending proceeding is one that would make the person unfit` IS su
        `a criminal investigation on suspicion of an offence is under way` IS FALSE

GIVETH A `Standing as to offences (ss 35 and 36)`
`ind-b clean standing` MEANS
    `ind-b standing: convicted` FALSE `, the conviction unfitting` FALSE `, charged` FALSE `, the charge unfitting` FALSE

GIVEN st IS A `Standing as to offences (ss 35 and 36)`, cf IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Person connected with a testing body`
`ind-b connected person: standing` st `, may be in conflict` cf MEANS
    `Person connected with a testing body` WITH
        `standing as to offences` IS st
        `may be in a conflict of interest, directly or indirectly` IS cf

GIVEN inc IS A BOOLEAN, reg IS A BOOLEAN, officer IS A `Person connected with a testing body`, pr IS A BOOLEAN, fu IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Corporation that would serve as a testing body`
`ind-b corporation: incorporated in Israel` inc `, registered in Israel` reg `, one officer` officer `, staffing proved` pr `, tender conditions` fu MEANS
    `Corporation that would serve as a testing body` WITH
        `incorporated in Israel` IS inc
        `registered in Israel` IS reg
        `the corporation itself` IS `ind-b connected person: standing` `ind-b clean standing` `, may be in conflict` FALSE
        `officers and controllers of the corporation` IS LIST officer
        `proved to the Minister's satisfaction that it employs testers in the fields and to the extent required` IS pr
        `the further conditions set in the tender or the terms of engagement are met, if any were set` IS fu
        `already a testing body within section 33` IS FALSE

GIVETH A `Person connected with a testing body`
`ind-b a clean officer` MEANS
    `ind-b connected person: standing` `ind-b clean standing` `, may be in conflict` FALSE

GIVEN st IS A `Standing as to offences (ss 35 and 36)`, cf IS A BOOLEAN, rg IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN, fu IS A BOOLEAN, rs IS A BOOLEAN, hr IS A BOOLEAN, rf IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Person to be authorised as a tester or an expert`
`ind-b person to authorise: standing` st `, may be in conflict` cf `, meets the regulations` rg `, found unfit` fu `, reasons given` rs `, hearing given` hr `, refused` rf MEANS
    `Person to be authorised as a tester or an expert` WITH
        `standing as to offences` IS st
        `may be in a conflict of interest, directly or indirectly` IS cf
        `meets the conditions set by regulations under section 60(1)(c), if the caller says` IS rg
        `the Minister found circumstances that make the person unfit to serve as a tester or an expert` IS fu
        `the Minister gave the person his reasons for refusing` IS rs
        `the person was given an opportunity to argue in writing` IS hr
        `the Minister refused to authorise the person` IS rf

GIVETH A `Tester or expert at work`
`ind-b an authorised tester at work` MEANS
    `Tester or expert at work` WITH
        `capacity` IS `acting as a tester`
        `holds an authorisation under section 36 that is in force` IS TRUE
        `acting to carry out an auxiliary test` IS TRUE
        `acting to give an expert opinion` IS FALSE
        `within the conditions and instructions in the instrument of authorisation` IS TRUE
        `the Law has commenced for the work on the system being tested` IS TRUE

GIVEN g IS A BOOLEAN, sh IS A BOOLEAN, wc IS A BOOLEAN, tb IS A BOOLEAN, dw IS A BOOLEAN, rq IS A BOOLEAN, ar IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Entry by a tester or an expert under section 37`
`ind-b entry: senior inspector's grounds` g `, authorisation shown` sh `, written consent` wc `, explained before consent` tb `, a dwelling` dw `, occupier asked` rq `, arranged in advance` ar MEANS
    `Entry by a tester or an expert under section 37` WITH
        `the senior inspector has reason to suppose that a person operating there does work on a cooling system without a licence or not in accordance with the conditions of his licence` IS g
        `the senior inspector has reason to suppose that a person operating there engages another in such work without a licence or not in accordance with the conditions of the licence` IS FALSE
        `showed the instrument of authorisation to the holder of the place` IS sh
        `the holder gave written consent to the entry` IS wc
        `the holder was told the purpose of the tests` IS TRUE
        `the holder was told of his right to refuse the tests` IS TRUE
        `the holder was told of his right to withdraw consent until the tests begin` IS TRUE
        `the holder was told all this before he gave consent` IS tb
        `the holder withdrew his consent before the tests began` IS FALSE
        `used as a dwelling` IS dw
        `the holder asked for the entry` IS rq
        `the entry was arranged with the holder in advance` IS ar

GIVEN h IS A BOOLEAN, f1 IS A BOOLEAN, f2 IS A BOOLEAN, f3 IS A BOOLEAN, f4 IS A BOOLEAN, f5 IS A BOOLEAN, dmd IS A MAYBE `Demand under section 39(b)`, met IS A BOOLEAN, imp IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Case for revoking or suspending an authorisation`
`ind-b case: hearing` h `, false or mistaken information` f1 `, a s.36 condition ceased` f2 `, a condition breached` f3 `, special circumstances` f4 `, poor work` f5 `, demand` dmd `, demand met` met `, compliance impossible` imp MEANS
    `Case for revoking or suspending an authorisation` WITH
        `the tester or expert was given an opportunity to argue in writing` IS h
        `the authorisation was granted on false or mistaken information` IS f1
        `a condition for the authorisation under section 36 ceased to hold` IS f2
        `a condition of the authorisation or an instruction under this Chapter was breached` IS f3
        `special circumstances make the tester or expert unfit to be one` IS f4
        `the work of the tester or expert is not done at a proper professional level` IS f5
        `the Minister demanded that the condition or instruction be met, or the defect corrected` IS dmd
        `the tester or expert met the demand in the manner and within the time directed` IS met
        `meeting the condition or instruction is impossible` IS imp

-- A demand made 1.3.2026 for 30 days: the time runs to 31.3.2026 (IL s.10(a)); decisions are on 1.6.2026.
GIVETH A MAYBE `Demand under section 39(b)`
`ind-b a demand of 1.3.2026 for 30 days` MEANS
    JUST (`Demand under section 39(b)` WITH `the demand was made on` IS YMD 2026 3 1, `the time directed for meeting it` IS `a number of days fixed by the Minister` 30)

GIVETH A `Calendar of rest days`
`ind-b no rest days` MEANS
    `Calendar of rest days` WITH `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS EMPTY

GIVEN c IS A `Case for revoking or suspending an authorisation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ind-b the Minister may revoke or suspend on 1.6.2026 in` c MEANS
    `s 39 — the Minister may revoke or suspend the authorisation` c (YMD 2026 6 1) `ind-b no rest days`

§§ `s.30 (I30-1 .. I30-8)`

#ASSERT `s 30(b) — the candidate may be authorised as an inspector` (`ind-b inspector candidate: Ministry employee` TRUE `, convicted` FALSE `, charged` FALSE `, unfit in the Minister's opinion` FALSE `, trained` TRUE `, further conditions` NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT `s 30(b) — the candidate may be authorised as an inspector` (`ind-b inspector candidate: Ministry employee` TRUE `, convicted` TRUE `, charged` FALSE `, unfit in the Minister's opinion` TRUE `, trained` TRUE `, further conditions` NOTHING)
-- I30-4: criminal proceedings pending, no conviction: s.30(b)(1) speaks only of conviction.
#ASSERT `s 30(b) — the candidate may be authorised as an inspector` (`ind-b inspector candidate: Ministry employee` TRUE `, convicted` FALSE `, charged` TRUE `, unfit in the Minister's opinion` FALSE `, trained` TRUE `, further conditions` NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT `s 30(b) — the candidate may be authorised as an inspector` (`ind-b inspector candidate: Ministry employee` TRUE `, convicted` FALSE `, charged` FALSE `, unfit in the Minister's opinion` FALSE `, trained` FALSE `, further conditions` NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT `s 30(b) — the candidate may be authorised as an inspector` (`ind-b inspector candidate: Ministry employee` TRUE `, convicted` FALSE `, charged` FALSE `, unfit in the Minister's opinion` FALSE `, trained` TRUE `, further conditions` (JUST FALSE))
#ASSERT `s 30(b) — the candidate may be authorised as an inspector` (`ind-b inspector candidate: Ministry employee` TRUE `, convicted` FALSE `, charged` FALSE `, unfit in the Minister's opinion` FALSE `, trained` TRUE `, further conditions` (JUST TRUE))
-- I30-8: an inspector authorised for some powers only may use only those.
#ASSERT `the inspector may use the power` (`ind-b inspector with powers` (LIST `require name, address and identification`) `, on duty` TRUE `, badge visible` TRUE `, certificate signed by the Minister` TRUE `, certificate demanded` FALSE `, shown` FALSE) `require name, address and identification`
#ASSERT NOT `the inspector may use the power` (`ind-b inspector with powers` (LIST `require name, address and identification`) `, on duty` TRUE `, badge visible` TRUE `, certificate signed by the Minister` TRUE `, certificate demanded` FALSE `, shown` FALSE) `enter a place to supervise`

§§ `s.31 (I31-1 .. I31-10)`

#ASSERT `the inspector may use the power` `ind-b a fully equipped inspector` `require name, address and identification`
#ASSERT `s 31(2) — the demand is one the inspector may make` `ind-b a fully equipped inspector` (`ind-b a demand for a document, the person concerned` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 31(2) — the demand is one the inspector may make` `ind-b a fully equipped inspector` (`ind-b a demand for a document, the person concerned` FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 31(3) — the inspector may enter the place` `ind-b a fully equipped inspector` (`ind-b place: grounds of unlicensed work` TRUE `, grounds of engaging the unlicensed` FALSE `, a dwelling` FALSE `, court order` FALSE `, occupier consents` FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 31(3) — the inspector may enter the place` `ind-b a fully equipped inspector` (`ind-b place: grounds of unlicensed work` FALSE `, grounds of engaging the unlicensed` TRUE `, a dwelling` FALSE `, court order` FALSE `, occupier consents` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 31(3) — the inspector may enter the place` `ind-b a fully equipped inspector` (`ind-b place: grounds of unlicensed work` FALSE `, grounds of engaging the unlicensed` FALSE `, a dwelling` FALSE `, court order` FALSE `, occupier consents` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 31(3) — the inspector may enter the place` `ind-b a fully equipped inspector` (`ind-b place: grounds of unlicensed work` TRUE `, grounds of engaging the unlicensed` FALSE `, a dwelling` TRUE `, court order` FALSE `, occupier consents` FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 31(3) — the inspector may enter the place` `ind-b a fully equipped inspector` (`ind-b place: grounds of unlicensed work` TRUE `, grounds of engaging the unlicensed` FALSE `, a dwelling` TRUE `, court order` TRUE `, occupier consents` FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 31(3) — the inspector may enter the place` `ind-b a fully equipped inspector` (`ind-b place: grounds of unlicensed work` TRUE `, grounds of engaging the unlicensed` FALSE `, a dwelling` TRUE `, court order` FALSE `, occupier consents` TRUE)
